{
  "title": "52: al-Toor الطور",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nوَالطُّوْرِۙ‏(1)\n\nBy the Mountain ‘Tur\nوَكِتٰبٍ مَّسْطُوْرٍۙ‏(2)\n\nAnd the Book written\nفِىْ رَقٍّ مَّنْشُوْرٍۙ‏(3)\n\nOn a lustrous Parchment outstretched\nوَالْبَيْتِ الْمَعْمُوْرِۙ‏(4)\n\nAnd by the House populated\nوَالسَّقْفِ الْمَرْفُوْعِۙ‏(5)\n\nAnd by the Roof elevated\nوَالْبَحْرِ الْمَسْجُوْرِۙ‏(6)\n\nAnd by the Sea boiling\nاِنَّ عَذَابَ رَبِّكَ لوَاقِعٌ ۙ‏(7)\n\nVerily the chastisement of thy Lord shall indeed come to pass\nمَّا لَهٗ مِنْ دَافِعٍۙ‏(8)\n\nThere is none to repel it\nيَّوْمَ تَمُوْرُ السَّمَآءُ مَوْرًا ۙ‏(9)\n\nOn the Day when the heaven shall reel a (Terrible) reeling\nوَّتَسِيْرُ الْجِبَالُ سَيْرًا ؕ‏(10)\n\nAnd the mountains shall fly an (awful) flight\nفَوَيْلٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُكَذِّبِيْنَۙ‏(11)\n\nWoe then that day unto those who belie the Truth\nالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ فِىْ خَوْضٍ يَّلْعَبُوْنَۘ‏(12)\n\nThose who, in vain sport do play\nيَوْمَ يُدَعُّوْنَ اِلٰى نَارِ جَهَنَّمَ دَعًّاؕ‏(13)\n\nThe Day on which they shall be driven unto the hell-fire with a violent drive\nهٰذِهِ النَّارُ الَّتِىْ كُنْتُمْ بِهَا تُكَذِّبُوْنَ‏(14)\n\n[And it shall be said unto them]: ‘This is the Fire which ye used to belie\nاَفَسِحْرٌ هٰذَاۤ اَمْ اَنْتُمْ لَا تُبْصِرُوْنَۚ‏(15)\n\nWhat! Is it sorcery then? Or ye see it not?\nاِصْلَوْهَا فَاصْبِرُوْۤا اَوْ لَا تَصْبِرُوْاۚ سَوَآءٌ عَلَيْكُمْؕ اِنَّمَا تُجْزَوْنَ مَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(16)\n\nEnter ye into it then be ye patient, or be ye not patient, alike shall it be unto you; certainly, shall ye be recompensed what ye used to do\nاِنَّ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ فِىْ جَنّٰتٍ وَّنَعِيْمٍۙ‏(17)\n\nVerily the pious ones shall be in the gardens amidst the bounties (therein)\nفٰكِهِيْنَ بِمَاۤ اٰتٰٮهُمْ رَبُّهُمْۚ وَوَقٰٮهُمْ رَبُّهُمْ عَذَابَ الْجَحِيْمِ‏(18)\n\nRejoicing in what gave them their Lord, and saved them their Lord from the chastisement of the Hell\nكُلُوْا وَاشْرَبُوْا هَنِٓيْئًا ۢ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَۙ‏(19)\n\n(It will be said unto them)’. “Eat ye and drink ye in health and delight for what ye used to do\nمُتَّكِئِيْنَ عَلٰى سُرُرٍ مَّصْفُوْفَةٍ ۚ وَزَوَّجْنٰهُمْ بِحُوْرٍ عِيْنٍ‏(20)\n\nReclining on thrones ranged; And We will unite them with Huries (maidens pure) with large (lovely) eyes\nوَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَاتَّبَعَتْهُمْ ذُرِّيَّتُهُمْ بِاِيْمَانٍ اَلْحَقْنَا بِهِمْ ذُرِّيَّتَهُمْ وَمَاۤ اَلَتْنٰهُمْ مِّنْ عَمَلِهِمْ مِّنْ شَىْءٍؕ كُلُّ امْرِیءٍۢ بِمَا كَسَبَ رَهِيْنٌ‏(21)\n\nAnd those who believe and follow them their offspring in faith, We will unite with them their offspring and We will lessen not unto them aught of their (good) deeds; Every man shall for what he hath wrought, be responsible\nوَاَمْدَدْنٰهُمْ بِفَاكِهَةٍ وَّلَحْمٍ مِّمَّا يَشْتَهُوْنَ‏(22)\n\nAnd We will provide with fruits and flesh of what they desire\nيَتَنَازَعُوْنَ فِيْهَا كَاْسًا لَّا لَغْوٌ فِيْهَا وَلَا تَاْثِيْمٌ‏(23)\n\nThey shall pass therein to one another a cup wherein shall not be any vanity nor a sin\nوَيَطُوْفُ عَلَيْهِمْ غِلْمَانٌ لَّهُمْ كَاَنَّهُمْ لُؤْلُؤٌ مَّكْنُوْنٌ‏(24)\n\nAnd there shall go around them (serving them) youths (handsome) as if they are imbedded pearls\nوَاَقْبَلَ بَعْضُهُمْ عَلٰى بَعْضٍ يَّتَسَآءَلُوْنَ‏(25)\n\nAnd some shall accost the others making mutual enquiries\nقَالُوْۤا اِنَّا كُنَّا قَبْلُ فِىْۤ اَهْلِنَا مُشْفِقِيْنَ‏(26)\n\nThey will say: ‘Verily we feared ere (this) in regard to our families\nفَمَنَّ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْنَا وَوَقٰٮنَا عَذَابَ السَّمُوْمِ‏(27)\n\nBut God hath bestowed His grace on us, and He hath saved us from the chastisement of the scorching wind\nاِنَّا كُنَّا مِنْ قَبْلُ نَدْعُوْهُ ؕ اِنَّهٗ هُوَ الْبَرُّ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(28)\n\nVerily, we used ere this to call upon Him; Verily, He is the Benign, the Most Merciful\nفَذَكِّرْ فَمَاۤ اَنْتَ بِنِعْمَتِ رَبِّكَ بِكَاهِنٍ وَّلَا مَجْنُوْنٍؕ‏(29)\n\nSo thou remind on (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) for thou, by the grace of thy Lord (on thee), art neither a soothsayer, nor a mad man\nاَمْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ شَاعِرٌ نَّتَرَبَّصُ بِهٖ رَيْبَ الْمَنُوْنِ‏(30)\n\nOr say they (about thee O’ Our Apostle!) ‘A poet (is he)! Let us wait for him some fatal adversity (drawn) by time!\nقُلْ تَرَبَّصُوْا فَاِنِّىْ مَعَكُمْ مِّنَ الْمُتَرَبِّصِيْنَ ؕ‏(31)\n\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!). “Wait ye, and verily I too with you am of those who wait\nاَمْ تَاْمُرُهُمْ اَحْلَامُهُمْ بِهٰذَآ اَمْ هُمْ قَوْمٌ طَاغُوْنَۚ‏(32)\n\nOr is it that bid them their deliberations, to do this, or are they an inordinate people?\nاَمْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ تَقَوَّلَهٗ ۚ بَلْ لَّا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ ۚ‏(33)\n\nOr say they (that): ‘He hath forged it (the Qur’an)? Nay! they believe not\nفَلْيَاْتُوْا بِحَدِيْثٍ مِّثْلِهٖۤ اِنْ كَانُوْا صٰدِقِيْنَؕ‏(34)\n\nLet them then bring a dis-course like unto it, if they be truthful\nاَمْ خُلِقُوْا مِنْ غَيْرِ شَىْءٍ اَمْ هُمُ الْخٰلِقُوْنَؕ‏(35)\n\nOr were they created by nothing? Or are they themselves the creators?\nاَمْ خَلَقُوا السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَۚ بَلْ لَّا يُوْقِنُوْنَؕ‏(36)\n\nOr created they the heavens and the earth? Nay! they have no certainty\nاَمْ عِنْدَهُمْ خَزَآئِنُ رَبِّكَ اَمْ هُمُ الْمُصَۜيْطِرُوْنَؕ‏(37)\n\nOr with them are the treasures of thy Lord, Or hold they the absolute authority?\nاَمْ لَهُمْ سُلَّمٌ يَّسْتَمِعُوْنَ فِيْهِ ۚ فَلْيَاْتِ مُسْتَمِعُهُمْ بِسُلْطٰنٍ مُّبِيْنٍؕ‏(38)\n\nOr for them is a ladder by which they can (climb up into the heaven and) listen (to the angels)? Then let the listener of theirs bring a proof manifest\nاَمْ لَهُ الْبَنٰتُ وَلَكُمُ الْبَنُوْنَؕ‏(39)\n\nOr for Him are daughters and for ye sons?\nاَمْ تَسْئَلُهُمْ اَجْرًا فَهُمْ مِّنْ مَّغْرَمٍ مُّثْقَلُوْنَؕ‏(40)\n\nOr thou asketh of them any recompense, that they are burdened with the weight of debt?\nاَمْ عِنْدَهُمُ الْغَيْبُ فَهُمْ يَكْتُبُوْنَؕ‏(41)\n\nOr with them is the unseen that they write it down?\nاَمْ يُرِيْدُوْنَ كَيْدًاؕ فَالَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا هُمُ الْمَكِيْدُوْنَؕ‏(42)\n\nOr intend they to lay snares for thee? But those who disbelieve are themselves the snared ones\nاَمْ لَهُمْ اِلٰهٌ غَيْرُ اللّٰهِؕ سُبْحٰنَ اللّٰهِ عَمَّا يُشْرِكُوْنَ‏(43)\n\nOr for them is a god other than God? Hallowed is God from what they associate (with Him)\nوَاِنْ يَّرَوْا كِسْفًا مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ سَاقِطًا يَّقُوْلُوْا سَحَابٌ مَّرْكُوْمٌ‏(44)\n\nAnd if they see a portion of the heaven coming down, they would say: ‘(they are) clouds piled up\nفَذَرْهُمْ حَتّٰى يُلٰقُوْا يَوْمَهُمُ الَّذِىْ فِيْهِ يُصْعَقُوْنَۙ‏(45)\n\nLeave them then until they encounter the Day of theirs where-in they shall be smitten (with terror) to swoon\nيَوْمَ لَا يُغْنِىْ عَنْهُمْ كَيْدُهُمْ شَيْئًا وَّلَا هُمْ يُنْصَرُوْنَؕ‏(46)\n\nA day wherein their devices shall avail them not aught, nor shall they be helped\nوَاِنَّ لِلَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا عَذَابًا دُوْنَ ذٰلِكَ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(47)\n\nAnd verily for those who did injustice there shall be a chastisement besides that, but most of them know it not\nوَاصْبِرْ لِحُكْمِ رَبِّكَ فَاِنَّكَ بِاَعْيُنِنَا وَسَبِّحْ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّكَ حِيْنَ تَقُوْمُۙ‏(48)\n\nAnd wait thou patiently for the command of thy Lord, for verily thou art before Our eyes, and celebrate thou the praise of thy Lord when thou risest\nوَمِنَ الَّيْلِ فَسَبِّحْهُ وَاِدْبَارَ النُّجُوْمِ‏(49)\n\nAnd in the night too, celebrate thou His Glory and at the setting of the stars",
  "merits": "Surah al-Toor (The Mountain)\nThis Surah has 49 verses and it was revealed in Makkah. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said that the one who recites this Surah will be kept safe from the wrath and punishment of Allah (s.w.t.).\nImam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that the recitation of this Surah brings good fortune to the reciter and constant recitation by those who have been imprisoned secures an early release from bondage. Surah al-Toor, if recited or kept as a talisman, keeps children in good health."
}
